WEBVTT

00:00:00.730 --> 00:00:03.380
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:05.850
Go, Decode Talker!

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:07.820
Decode End!

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:09.860
Great Ogre!

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:11.840
Ogre Axe!

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:25.980
I lost!

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:32.030
Go Onizuka...  He was a formidable opponent.

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:39.150
There will come a time when we won't be 
enough to fight the Knights of Hanoi.

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:42.350
So if he can fight on our side...

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:48.120
The fight against the Knights 
of Hanoi is life-or-death.

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:51.500
I don't want to involve him 
in that kind of dueling.

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:09.750
I run Across the universe

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:12.920
At the speed of light

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:14.790
Begin Loading

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:18.520
Open the door of dreams

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:22.090
VRAINS spreads

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:25.200
Believe in myself

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:28.730
VRAINS continues

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:34.040
The circuit draws the future

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:38.110
I'll grab it with my own hands  Yeah

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:39.710
Access!

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:42.410
Start swirling, Data Storm!

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:44.020
I'm now With the Wind

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.320
Link with my soul

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:49.090
Speed up, Data Storm!

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:50.820
Now Win the Race

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:53.660
Connected world

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:57.160
No matter when

00:01:57.410 --> 00:02:00.530
Nothing is impossible

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:04.670
Strive for hope

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:09.240
And ride the wind!

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:28.260
Everyone!  Here I go!

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:37.240
Get ready!  This is the finale!

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:39.200
Damn!

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:44.640
Trickstar Holly Angel attacks you directly!

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:52.200
That's the end!

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:56.550
You all behave until my next live show!

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:58.520
See ya!  Bye bye!

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:01.490
Bye bye!

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:09.350
You have logged out.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:37.030
Unbelievable.  It's impossible.

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:38.090
What is?

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:39.020
Look at this.

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:43.470
Aoi Zaizen, 16 years old.

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:48.070
Sister-in-law of Akira Zaizen, SOL 
Technologies' Security Manager.

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:51.440
And Blue Angel's true identity.

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:53.410
Oh really?

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:55.040
And?

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:56.410
"And?"

00:03:56.410 --> 00:03:59.420
Notice something about her school uniform?

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:02.800
Can't see what's in front of your nose.

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:04.070
She goes to my school?

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:05.200
That's right.

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:08.660
Yusaku, I thought that 
if you get to know her...

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:10.870
...you can get information

00:04:10.870 --> 00:04:16.380
about your lost memories and my brother 
from SOL Technologies' Zaizen.

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:18.140
But that's impossible.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:20.740
Why is that impossible?

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:24.030
Because we're talking about Yusaku here.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:27.350
Can you imagine Yusaku talking to a girl?

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:32.380
You're right.  That's impossible to imagine.

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:35.710
Right?  Impossible.  Impossible impossible.

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:39.340
Totally impossible.  Not 
possible.  Never possible.

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:45.800
So it's possible?

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:48.940
I didn't know you liked picking up girls.

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:49.880
I don't.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:57.830
Anyway, school is full of people who dress 
the same, so it's hard to tell them apart-

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:59.140
Hurry up and find her.

00:04:59.140 --> 00:04:59.880
Yeah yeah.

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:03.570
Let me see...

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:12.800
Nope.  Nope.  Nope.  Nope.

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:16.760
Found her!

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:32.480
Combining the data of each of her 
parts, I classify her as beautiful.

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:34.450
Stay quiet and keep watch.

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:48.200
Duel Club?

00:05:49.630 --> 00:05:51.060
Fujiki!

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:54.730
Who are you again?

00:05:54.730 --> 00:05:57.460
Who?  We just talked the other day!

00:05:57.460 --> 00:05:59.900
Shima!  Naoki Shima!

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:03.540
Oh yeah.  We're in the same class, right?

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:09.400
Anyway, what are you doing 
here wearing a Duel Disk?

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:10.210
Well...

00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:13.920
I know!  You came to join the Duel Club!

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:16.200
Me?  Duel Club?

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:19.890
Oh!  I didn't know this 
room was the Duel Club!

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:22.060
Stop acting dumb!

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:27.920
This place isn't for a loser who 
has no interest in LINK VRAINS!

00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:30.140
What's the ruckus, Shima?

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:32.380
I can hear you from inside.

00:06:32.380 --> 00:06:34.700
President, I'm sorry.

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:36.020
It's his fault-

00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:39.560
It's fine.  New applicants 
are always welcome.

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:40.880
Please come in.

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:42.350
No, wait...

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:44.620
Okay!  Thank you!

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:46.320
How dare you...

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:51.060
I'm freshman Yusaku Fujiki.

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:53.660
I'm Hosoda, Club President.

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:55.620
I'm Tanaka.  Second year.

00:06:55.620 --> 00:06:57.400
I'm also second year.  Sato.

00:06:57.400 --> 00:06:59.420
I'm freshman Suzuki.

00:06:59.660 --> 00:07:01.400
I'm freshman Zaizen.

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:04.520
Do you want to see the new Duel Disk?

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:08.670
Oh!  The version with an AI that 
supports you during a duel.

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:10.380
You know a lot.

00:07:10.600 --> 00:07:12.860
Because Shima bragged about it.

00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:15.110
But he's not the only one who has it?

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:18.600
I never said that only I had it!

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:21.120
Stop trying to make me look bad!

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:25.290
Zaizen's brother is a big 
shot at SOL Technologies.

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:28.810
So they gave it to our club first!

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:35.270
Hey, new model!  How goes it?

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:37.080
Hello.

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:40.690
Good.  Always make sure to greet me.

00:07:40.690 --> 00:07:43.040
I don't know what you mean.

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:45.200
You have no social skills.

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:46.510
Unable to comprehend.

00:07:47.630 --> 00:07:48.490
Oh oh!

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:52.690
A card insertion-type Duel Disk?

00:07:52.690 --> 00:07:53.540
Yeah.

00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:55.650
It's the same as Playmaker's.

00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:58.620
Seriously, right?

00:07:58.840 --> 00:08:02.320
I think he's copying Playmaker.

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:06.980
But why does Playmaker use 
an old-type Duel Disk?

00:08:06.980 --> 00:08:11.240
It's sad.  He's behind the times.

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:13.380
Will you show me your deck?

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:16.240
That's rude, Zaizen.

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:18.580
A deck is a duelist's life.

00:08:18.910 --> 00:08:20.550
It's fine.  Take a look.

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:29.910
Thank you.

00:08:29.910 --> 00:08:31.030
Cutting in!

00:08:31.260 --> 00:08:33.070
Let me take a look.

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:38.000
What's with this?  What a lame deck!

00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:42.870
That's rude, Shima!

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:47.750
As a duelist, insulting 
another's deck is disgraceful!

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:51.340
I'm sorry, President.  I got caught up.

00:08:52.750 --> 00:08:54.840
I'm sorry I laughed.

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:58.000
It's fine.  Because you're right.

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:01.290
Let's start the meeting.

00:09:02.030 --> 00:09:05.660
First, let's check the Speed Duel rules.

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:09.620
The first difference between 
Master Duels and Speed Duels:

00:09:09.620 --> 00:09:14.730
There are only three Main Monster 
Zones and Spell & Trap Zones.

00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:18.250
What are the other differences?

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:19.540
Anyone?

00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:20.970
Yes, Tanaka.

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:23.840
You start with four cards in your hand.

00:09:24.190 --> 00:09:26.940
And there's no Main Phase 2.

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:28.750
Hey, lame-o.

00:09:29.530 --> 00:09:32.610
Good idea changing your 
deck with a dummy deck.

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:34.400
Be quiet.

00:09:53.740 --> 00:09:56.410
Welcome home, Aoi.

00:09:56.700 --> 00:10:01.150
Your brother can't come home 
today again due to work.

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:12.480
There are rumors that SOL Technologies 
initiated the duel between Go Onizuka and Playmaker.

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:14.800
Ask our PR department.

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:18.320
Is this a new business strategy?

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:19.440
No comment.

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:22.880
Will the next match be 
Blue Angel vs Playmaker?

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:24.240
No.

00:10:40.940 --> 00:10:42.300
Brother?

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:44.000
Aoi.

00:10:44.570 --> 00:10:47.620
Good evening.  I saw you on the news.

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:50.680
Why are you unhappy?

00:10:51.890 --> 00:10:54.960
How long will you pretend to be an idol?

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:55.970
Well...

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:58.220
Speed Duels are dangerous.

00:10:58.220 --> 00:11:00.360
If you make a mistake, you may die.

00:11:00.360 --> 00:11:01.710
Stop immediately.

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:03.940
Yes, Brother.

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:07.160
I'm saying this because I care about you.

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:08.410
Understand?

00:11:08.620 --> 00:11:10.780
I understand, Brother.

00:11:11.060 --> 00:11:15.750
Listen.  No one can find 
out that you're Blue Angel.

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:17.560
I know.

00:11:17.560 --> 00:11:19.940
Think of my position.

00:11:20.270 --> 00:11:22.500
Yes, Brother.

00:11:25.240 --> 00:11:27.420
Do you really understand?

00:11:29.780 --> 00:11:34.180
I just want my brother to 
know that I can hold my own.

00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:39.640
Will the next match be 
Blue Angel vs Playmaker?

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:41.070
No.

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:51.840
I'll do it for you, Brother.

00:11:54.680 --> 00:11:56.360
Into the VRAINS.

00:12:10.640 --> 00:12:13.140
Blue Angel, will you duel me?

00:12:13.410 --> 00:12:14.370
Pass!

00:12:14.910 --> 00:12:16.920
Blue Angel, will-

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:17.830
Pass!

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:19.830
Blue Angel-

00:12:19.830 --> 00:12:20.910
Pass!

00:12:21.820 --> 00:12:26.360
If I defeat Playmaker, my brother 
will know I can hold my own.

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:30.090
Look!  It's Blue Angel!

00:12:30.460 --> 00:12:31.860
Roll the camera!

00:12:35.830 --> 00:12:36.800
Hi!

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:39.800
Everyone, I'm here!

00:12:40.240 --> 00:12:43.190
You there!  And you over there!

00:12:43.190 --> 00:12:44.980
Watch!

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:52.920
I declare that I, Blue Angel, 
will duel Playmaker and win!

00:12:52.920 --> 00:12:54.950
Blue Angel vs Playmaker!

00:12:54.950 --> 00:12:56.780
Awesome!  When?

00:12:56.780 --> 00:12:59.430
First Go Onizuka, now Blue Angel!

00:12:59.640 --> 00:13:01.870
Come out, Playmaker!

00:13:01.870 --> 00:13:03.000
C'mon!

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:05.400
I know you're watching, Playmaker!

00:13:05.400 --> 00:13:08.080
Accept my challenge!

00:13:08.080 --> 00:13:10.870
Why is she so fired up?

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:12.980
Just duel her.

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:14.310
I refuse.

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:20.340
#1: I only approached Aoi Zaizen to 
get a lead on my stolen memories.

00:13:20.640 --> 00:13:24.520
#2: I only fight the Knights of Hanoi.

00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:28.000
#3: Blue Angel isn't Hanoi.

00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:31.800
People will say that you're a scared coward.

00:13:31.800 --> 00:13:33.590
They can say whatever they like.

00:13:33.840 --> 00:13:36.590
Playmaker!  Duel me!

00:13:39.100 --> 00:13:41.030
This is getting interesting.

00:13:41.240 --> 00:13:45.500
I think we can use her, Revolver.

00:13:45.500 --> 00:13:50.910
There you go!  Blue Angel 
made a public challenge!

00:13:50.910 --> 00:13:54.560
If he doesn't accept, he's not a man!

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:57.140
Show up, Playmaker!

00:14:00.780 --> 00:14:03.520
Call me if Playmaker shows up.

00:14:03.520 --> 00:14:05.930
I have another assignment-

00:14:11.050 --> 00:14:14.030
Playmaker hasn't shown up.

00:14:16.220 --> 00:14:18.700
Who are you?  Are you a Knight of Hanoi?

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:23.640
Hello.  Duel world's idol, Blue Angel.

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:38.620
Your passion towards Playmaker...

00:14:40.120 --> 00:14:42.460
...has deeply impressed me.

00:14:42.840 --> 00:14:46.360
I'm a fan of yours.

00:14:46.640 --> 00:14:48.930
A passionate fan.

00:14:49.140 --> 00:14:51.940
You're obviously lying!

00:14:51.940 --> 00:14:54.940
I'm not lying.

00:14:54.940 --> 00:14:59.680
I just want you to defeat Playmaker.

00:15:06.770 --> 00:15:10.680
That card will open a 
door deep in your heart.

00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:14.130
A key that frees your hidden desires.

00:15:17.340 --> 00:15:19.780
Good luck.

00:15:37.960 --> 00:15:40.930
What am I doing here?

00:15:49.790 --> 00:15:53.530
Sigh...  This is worse than I thought.

00:15:53.530 --> 00:15:54.530
What is?

00:15:54.530 --> 00:15:57.580
You're getting hammered on the net.

00:15:57.880 --> 00:16:00.280
“Is Playmaker a chicken?”

00:16:00.870 --> 00:16:03.500
“Disappointed he didn't 
accept the challenge.”

00:16:03.500 --> 00:16:08.010
“A true duelist accepts all challenges."

00:16:08.010 --> 00:16:09.640
Also...

00:16:09.640 --> 00:16:10.750
That's enough.

00:16:11.090 --> 00:16:12.930
Oh my.  Are you mad?

00:16:12.930 --> 00:16:14.790
You actually care!

00:16:14.790 --> 00:16:17.080
Are your feelings hurt?

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:19.080
Quiet!  She's here.

00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:25.160
Yusaku Fujiki, right?  Good morning.

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:28.170
Y-Yeah.  Good morning.

00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:32.140
Hey, new model!  How goes it?

00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:35.240
Humph!  Stop acting like we're friends!

00:16:37.280 --> 00:16:40.340
Something is weird.

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:46.280
Why did you want to join the Duel Club?

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:47.480
Because...

00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:51.160
Don't say it's because you love to duel.

00:16:53.320 --> 00:16:57.130
What Shima said about 
your brother yesterday...

00:16:58.540 --> 00:17:00.130
You too, huh?

00:17:01.160 --> 00:17:04.420
"Can I get the new Duel Disk first?"

00:17:04.420 --> 00:17:07.260
Or "Can I get a job at SOL when I graduate?"

00:17:07.260 --> 00:17:10.420
The only reasons why people approach me.

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:11.480
I...

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:12.940
Don't even try.

00:17:14.660 --> 00:17:18.150
My brother doesn't trust me.

00:17:26.740 --> 00:17:28.510
Hey, Yusaku.

00:17:28.510 --> 00:17:30.130
I need to talk to you-

00:17:30.130 --> 00:17:30.930
Be quiet.

00:17:30.930 --> 00:17:34.110
Hey!  Suit yourself.

00:17:40.480 --> 00:17:41.370
Hold up!

00:17:41.600 --> 00:17:43.610
Idiot!  You're too loud!

00:17:43.610 --> 00:17:45.580
A Knight of Hanoi has appeared!

00:17:45.930 --> 00:17:46.990
What?

00:17:47.640 --> 00:17:53.770
The relationship between the lens of a cat's 
eye and quantum mechanical algorithms...

00:17:53.770 --> 00:17:58.060
...was advocated by German physicist 
Professor Werner in 1974-

00:17:58.060 --> 00:17:59.020
Excuse me!

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:02.990
I don't feel well.  Can 
I go to the infirmary?

00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:21.580
Deck set!  Into the VRAINS!

00:18:56.780 --> 00:18:59.060
Where's the Knight of Hanoi?

00:18:59.060 --> 00:19:01.920
This is the correct coordinates.

00:19:07.380 --> 00:19:08.830
Blue Angel.

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:11.060
You finally made your decision.

00:19:11.060 --> 00:19:13.360
Decided what?

00:19:13.360 --> 00:19:16.600
Enough!  Still playing dumb?

00:19:17.080 --> 00:19:18.300
Playing dumb?

00:19:18.520 --> 00:19:20.770
You invited me here.

00:19:22.740 --> 00:19:26.710
I'll duel you right now.
- Playmaker

00:19:27.320 --> 00:19:29.400
I invited you?

00:19:30.400 --> 00:19:32.450
Ai, is this your doing?

00:19:32.660 --> 00:19:34.100
Yes!

00:19:34.100 --> 00:19:35.550
You tricked me?

00:19:35.550 --> 00:19:37.390
What are you talking about?

00:19:37.390 --> 00:19:38.930
I didn't trick you.

00:19:39.300 --> 00:19:41.930
You said the Knight of Hanoi was here.

00:19:41.930 --> 00:19:44.400
And there she is.  Right in front of you.

00:19:45.760 --> 00:19:46.660
Can't be...

00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:48.460
Blue Angel...

00:19:48.460 --> 00:19:52.640
Even though it's faint, I sense 
Hanoi in Aoi Zaizen's deck.

00:19:59.280 --> 00:20:01.710
So that's what you sensed earlier.

00:20:01.710 --> 00:20:05.320
I tried to tell you, but you wouldn't listen.

00:20:05.560 --> 00:20:08.320
But why did she join the Knights of Hanoi?

00:20:08.320 --> 00:20:09.390
Who knows.

00:20:09.390 --> 00:20:13.010
Maybe they're using her 
as a lure to hook you.

00:20:13.010 --> 00:20:14.560
A lure to hook me?

00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:18.260
A big timer may be backing her.

00:20:18.660 --> 00:20:21.020
What will you do, Playmaker?

00:20:21.020 --> 00:20:23.970
I thought you were going to defeat all Hanoi.

00:20:39.750 --> 00:20:42.130
C'mon, everybody!

00:20:42.130 --> 00:20:47.360
Blue Angel vs Playmaker is 
finally starting!  Yeah!

00:20:47.370 --> 00:20:53.060
The greatest battle in history is here!

00:20:53.280 --> 00:20:56.070
Yusaku!  Why are you dueling Blue Angel?

